<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Guérande</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Guérande is a walled town in the Loire-Atlantique <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, on the peninsula between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/loire">Loire</a> estuary and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vilaine">Vilaine</a>. Its salt marshes have produced sea salt since the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>, a major export of the Duchy of Brittany. Two treaties signed there, in 1365 and 1381, settled the Breton succession and the duke's relations with France, and its fifteenth-century ramparts survive.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/guerande.jpg" alt="Guérande" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gab44 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Guerande44.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
